-* `DPLD_REQUIRE_SCAN` and `GITLEAKS_BIN` are read only by `tests/test_hygiene.py`. `DPLD_REQUIRE_SCAN` acts on any non-empty value (even `0`): it makes a missing gitleaks program a failure and also scans the git history. `GITLEAKS_BIN` is the path of the gitleaks program (if it is not set, the program is looked up on `PATH`). A hand-run secret scan must start in the repository root (`gitleaks dir .`, as `.github/workflows/lint.yml` does): the allowance for the lock files (`requirements-*.txt`) and the workflow files in `.gitleaks.toml` is anchored at the root, so a scan given an absolute folder path reports them.
+* `DPLD_*` names belong to this project (DPLD stands for duplicate-proof lead desk, the repository name). `DPLD_REQUIRE_SCAN` and `GITLEAKS_BIN` are read only by `tests/test_hygiene.py`. `DPLD_REQUIRE_SCAN` acts on any non-empty value (even `0`): it makes a missing gitleaks program a failure and also scans the git history. `GITLEAKS_BIN` is the path of the gitleaks program (if it is not set, the program is looked up on `PATH`). A hand-run secret scan must start in the repository root (`gitleaks dir .`, as `.github/workflows/lint.yml` does): the allowance for the lock files (`requirements-*.txt`) and the workflow files in `.gitleaks.toml` is anchored at the root, so a scan given an absolute folder path reports them.
 * `LEAD_DESK_PATH_ROOTS` (read by the load tools, `scripts/n8n_api.py import` and `tools/scrub_n8n_export.py`; not by the desk): extra folders, separated by `:` (`;` on Windows), where those tools may read and write the files named on their command line. Without it only the folder the tool was started in, the repository folder and the system temporary folder are allowed (`load_tools/README.md`). Not affected: `scripts/run_real_check.py`, which reads the config you give it from any folder (a file in a folder you can list), and the files named inside that config (`docs/real-services.md`, "Where the files may be").
 * `DPLD_REQUIRE_DEMO` is read only by `tests/conftest.py`. With `DPLD_REQUIRE_DEMO=1` a checkout that has no `demo_only` folder stops the test run at the start (exit code 2) instead of skipping the test files that need it (the workflows `lint.yml` and `sonar.yml` both set it to 1 for their test step, so a lost folder stops the run there). Without it a missing folder skips each such test file as one item and the other files still run.
